+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="titan">Titan Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="titan/grammar.md">titan/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: Right-headed compounding; <em>Uld-</em> facility prefix;
+<em>-ir</em> animate/giant suffix; <em>Gor-</em> "dark" prefix;
+<em>-shalach</em> "rend" root. Titan syntax is entirely unknown — only one
+untranslated phrase exists. All constructions below are compound juxtapositions
+using attested morphemes.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ti1</td>
+  <td>Aes-ir, Kalim-dor.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈeɪsɪr ˈkælɪmdɔːr/</td>
+  <td>Storm-giants, starlight-land.</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Aesir</em> (Storm Giants) + attested <em>Kalimdor</em> (Land of Eternal Starlight); juxtaposition of two confirmed compounds</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ti2</td>
+  <td>Uld-aman, Uld-uar.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈʌldɑmɑn ˈʌlduːɑr/</td>
+  <td>City-vault, city-fortress.</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Uldaman</em> + attested <em>Ulduar</em>; <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes the <em>Uld-</em> prefix can be understood as a free morpheme meaning "city/facility"</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ti3</td>
+  <td>Gor-shalach, Gor-ribal.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɡɔːrˈʃælɑːk ˈɡɔːrɪbɑːl/</td>
+  <td>Dark-render, dark-seether.</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Gorshalach</em> + attested <em>Gorribal</em>; both use <em>Gor-</em> "dark" prefix (RPG); juxtaposition of two weapon names</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ti4</td>
+  <td>Van-ir, Uld-ir.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈvɑːnɪr ˈʌldɪr/</td>
+  <td>Earth-giants, city-[suffix].</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Vanir</em> + attested <em>Uldir</em>; <strong>speculative</strong> — the <em>-ir</em> in <em>Uldir</em> may or may not be the same animate suffix as in <em>Vanir</em></td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ti5</td>
+  <td>Khaz-goroth, Khaz-mul.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/kæzˈɡɔːroʊθ kæzˈmuːl/</td>
+  <td>Forge-world, forge-[chamber].</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Khaz'goroth</em> + attested <em>Khaz'mul</em>; <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes <em>Khaz</em> = "forge/shape" is a free root</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Ti6</td>
+  <td>Aes-dor.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈeɪsdɔːr/</td>
+  <td>Storm-land.</td>
+  <td>Compound of attested <em>Aes</em> ("storm") + attested <em>-dor</em> ("land"); <strong>highly speculative</strong> — assumes both morphemes can combine productively</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="vrykul">Vrykul Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="vrykul/grammar.md">vrykul/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: Imperative + conjunction + imperative (battle cry pattern);
+<em>-heim</em> home/realm suffix; <em>-jar</em> army/host suffix;
+<em>Val-</em> slain/chosen prefix; compounding pattern.
+Vrykul has several attested translated phrases, providing a stronger basis for
+construction than most WoW languages.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>V1</td>
+  <td>Rualg nja gaborr, Valarjar!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈruɑlɡ njɑ ɡɑˈbɔr ˈvɑlɑɾjɑɾ/</td>
+  <td>Stand and die, Army of the Chosen!</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Rualg nja gaborr</em> (Stand and die!) + attested vocative <em>Valarjar</em></td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>V2</td>
+  <td>Ugglin oo bjorr, Drottinn!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈʊɡlɪn oʊ bjɔr ˈdɾɔtɪn/</td>
+  <td>Speak or perish, Lord!</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Ugglin oo bjorr</em> (Speak or perish!) + attested title <em>Drottinn</em> (Lord)</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>V3</td>
+  <td>Val-halas, Ymir-jar.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈvɑlhɑlɑs ˈyːmɪɾjɑɾ/</td>
+  <td>Hall of the Slain, Ymir's Army.</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Valhalas</em> (Halls of Valor) + attested <em>Ymirjar</em> (Ymir's army); juxtaposition of two attested compounds</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>V4</td>
+  <td>Geirr-vif, Jotun-heim.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈɡɛɪɾːvɪf ˈjoːtʊnhaɪm/</td>
+  <td>Spear-wife, Home of the Giants.</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Geirrivif</em> (Spear-Wife) + attested <em>Jotunheim</em> (Home of the Giants); <strong>speculative</strong> juxtaposition</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>V5</td>
+  <td>Tiris-fal.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈtɪɾɪsfɑl/</td>
+  <td>Tyr's Fall.</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Tirisfal</em> (Tyr's Fall); this is a canon form, shown here to illustrate the compound pattern <em>Tiris</em> (Tyr) + <em>-fal</em> (fall)</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>V6</td>
+  <td>Bjorn-harta nja mord-vig!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈbjɔːɾnhɑrtɑ njɑ ˈmɔɾdvɪɡ/</td>
+  <td>Bear-heart and murder-battle!</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Bjornharta</em> + attested conjunction <em>nja</em> + speculative compound <em>mord-vig</em> (murder-battle); <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes <em>nja</em> can join noun phrases</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="nazja">Nazja Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="nazja/grammar.md">nazja/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: <em>-dorei</em> ethnonym suffix (shared with Darnassian);
+<em>-tar / -atar</em> city/domain suffix; apostrophe morpheme boundary;
+imperative-initial constructions. Nazja syntax is poorly attested — most
+known forms are battle cries and invocations.</p>
