+Proto-Elven, not an independent development. Nazja is especially notable: nearly all
+multi-morpheme naga names use apostrophes (more consistently than Darnassian), and the
+hyphen appears in battle cries (<em>Ash-thero-sauguine</em>) mirroring Darnassian
+phrase-level boundaries (<em>Andu-falah-dor</em>). This is a shared <em>graphological</em>
 cognate — a feature of the writing system preserved across all daughter languages.</p>
 
