+## The War Within (2024): Earthen and Khaz Algar
+
+*The War Within* expansion introduces the subterranean continent of **Khaz Algar** and the **Earthen** as a playable race. The Earthen are the stone progenitors of Dwarves, and their naming patterns in TWW provide new Dwarven/Earthen vocabulary.
+
+### Khaz Algar Place Names
+
+| Name | IPA | Analysis | Notes |
+|------|-----|----------|-------|
+| Khaz Algar | /kæz ˈælgɑːr/ | *Khaz-* (forge/craft) + *Algar* (uncertain) | The subterranean continent named after the Titan Khaz'goroth. The *Khaz-* element confirms this as a Titan-derived toponym, parallel to *Khaz Modan* (Mountain of Khaz). *Algar* may mean "deep" or "below" or may be a proper name. |
+| Isle of Dorn | /dɔːrn/ | *Dorn-* possibly related to Titan *-dor* (land) | Surface zone. *Dorn* / *Dor-n* could be *-dor* + *-n* suffix. |
+| Dornogal | /ˈdɔːrnəɡɑːl/ | *Dorn-* + *-ogal* (?) | Earthen capital city. *Dorn-* may be the same root as "Isle of Dorn." *-ogal* is unexplained but parallels *-agal* in other titan-forged suffixes. |
+| Ringing Deeps | — | Common/English name | Underground zone. |
+| Hallowfall | — | Common/English name | Underground cavern zone. |
+| Gundargaz | /ˈɡʊndɑːrɡæz/ | *Gun-* + *-dar-* + *-gaz* (?) | Machine Speakers settlement. The name shows Dwarven/Earthen phonological patterns (guttural stops, heavy consonant clusters). |
+| Deepforge Golemworks | — | Common/English compound | Abandoned war golem facility. |
+| Coreway | — | Common/English compound | Large access tunnel connecting surface to underground. |
+
+### Earthen Personal Names (The War Within)
+
+| Name | IPA | Affiliation | Notes |
+|------|-----|-------------|-------|
+| Baelgrim | /ˈbeɪlɡrɪm/ | Stormriders (Stormward) | Contains *Bael-* (cf. Dwarven *Bael'dun* = "stone/earth"?) + *-grim* (cf. Vrykul *-grim* = "mask/fierce" in *Bjarngrim*). If *Bael-* = "stone/earth" and *-grim* = "fierce/helmet," then *Baelgrim* = "Stone-fierce" — a fitting name for a military leader. |
+| Merrix | /ˈmɛrɪks/ | Oathsworn (Councilward) | No clear morpheme decomposition. The *-rix* ending may be a title suffix (cf. Latin *-rix* feminine agent suffix), though this is a real-world parallel, not in-universe. |
+| Adelgonn | /əˈdɛlɡɒn/ | Unbound (Stoneward) | Possibly *Adel-* + *-gonn*. *Adel-* may relate to "noble" (cf. Old English *æþele*). *-gonn* is unexplained. |
+| Brinthe | /ˈbrɪnθə/ | Machine Speakers (High Speaker) | Contains the dental fricative /θ/, also found in Vrykul (*Thros*, *Thorim*). May reflect Titan substrate vocabulary. |
+| Eirich | /ˈaɪrɪk/ | Machine Speakers (former High Speaker) | Possibly related to Vrykul *Eyir* (Val'kyr goddess). Both contain the *Eir-* element. If related, this would demonstrate a shared Titan morpheme across Vrykul and Earthen. |
+| Lufsela | /ˈlʊfsɛlə/ | Stormriders (new Stormward) | No clear morpheme decomposition. |
+
+### Earthen Cultural Groups
+
+| Name | IPA | Notes |
+|------|-----|-------|
+| Stormriders | — | English designation; military earthen who ride stormrooks |
+| Oathsworn | — | English designation; earthen who follow Titan edicts |
+| Unbound | — | English designation; earthen who reject Titan edicts |
+| Machine Speakers | — | English designation; earthen who maintain ancient machinery |
+| Skardyn | /ˈskɑːrdɪn/ | Earthen corrupted by void magic; the *Skar-* element may relate to Vrykul *Skar-* (cf. *Skarvald*, *Voldskar*) |
+
+### Key Linguistic Observations from The War Within
+
+1. **Khaz Algar confirms *Khaz-* as a productive Titan-derived toponymic prefix.** With *Khaz Modan* (Dwarven kingdom) and *Khaz Algar* (subterranean continent), the *Khaz-* prefix now appears in three distinct place names, strengthening the inference that *Khaz-* = "forge/craft/shape" in the Titan-forged language family.
+
+2. **Earthen personal names differ from Dwarven personal names.** Dwarven names (Magni, Muradin, Brann, Moira) follow a Celtic/Norse short-name pattern. Earthen names (Baelgrim, Merrix, Adelgonn, Brinthe, Eirich, Lufsela) show a different pattern with longer, more complex names. This may reflect:
+   - Earthen retaining older titan-forged naming conventions while Dwarves developed simpler names after the Curse of Flesh
+   - Regional variation: Khaz Algar Earthen were isolated for millennia from Eastern Kingdoms Dwarves
+   - Blizzard design choice for TWW aesthetics
+
+3. **The *Bael-* element appears in both Earthen and Dwarven naming.** Earthen *Baelgrim* (Stormward) and Dwarven *Bael'dun* (dig site) share the *Bael-* root. If *Bael-* = "stone/earth," this demonstrates a shared morpheme between the two groups, consistent with their common Earthen ancestry.
+
+4. **The *Eir-* element may connect Earthen and Vrykul.** Earthen *Eirich* and Vrykul *Eyir* (Val'kyr goddess) both contain the *Eir-* element. In Norse mythology, *Eir* is a goddess of healing. If both languages preserve this as a Titan morpheme, it would demonstrate deep vocabulary retention across the titan-forged family.
+
+5. **Skardyn as a void-corrupted Earthen term.** The *Skar-* element in *Skardyn* parallels Vrykul *Skar-* in *Skarvald* and *Voldskar*. If *Skar-* = "dark/corrupt" or "shadow" in the titan-forged family, this would be a meaningful connection, though the sample size is too small to confirm.

