+<h2 id="titan-earthen">Titan &harr; Earthen Cross-Reference</h2>
+
+<p>Earthen is the closest living descendant of Titan. The Earthen were directly created by
+Khaz'goroth and, unlike Dwarves, have <strong>not undergone the Curse of Flesh</strong>
+(in Khaz Algar). Their language preserves more Titan morphemes and phonological features
+than any other titan-forged language. See <a href="earthen/description.md">earthen/description.md</a>
+for full documentation.</p>
+
+<h3>Shared Elements</h3>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Element</th><th>Titan Form</th><th>Earthen Form</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
+<tr class="shared">
+  <td><em>Khaz-</em></td>
+  <td><em>Khaz'goroth</em> (Shaper of Worlds), <em>Khaz'mul</em></td>
+  <td><em>Khaz Algar</em> (subterranean continent)</td>
+  <td>forge / craft / shape</td>
+  <td>Direct retention: Earthen preserve *Khaz-* as a productive toponymic prefix</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="shared">
+  <td><em>-dor</em> / <em>-dar</em></td>
+  <td><em>Kalimdor</em> = "Land of Eternal Starlight"</td>
+  <td><em>Dorn-</em> (Isle of Dorn), <em>-dar</em> (Beledar, Mereldar), <em>Dornogal</em></td>
+  <td>land / realm</td>
+  <td>Probable sound correspondence: Titan *-dor* → Earthen *-dar* / *Dorn-*; vowel raising /ɔ/ → /ɑ/ and optional final /n/</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="shared">
+  <td><em>Uld-</em></td>
+  <td><em>Ulduar</em>, <em>Uldum</em>, <em>Uldaman</em></td>
+  <td>Known through Uldaman (where Earthen were shaped)</td>
+  <td>city / facility</td>
+  <td>Direct Titan loanword; Earthen know the *Uld-* pattern through their origin at Uldaman</td>
+</tr>
+<tr class="shared">
+  <td>Right-headed compounding</td>
+  <td><em>Gor</em>+<em>shalach</em> = dark-render</td>
+  <td><em>Bael</em>+<em>grim</em> = stone-fierce (?)</td>
+  <td>modifier-head order</td>
+  <td>Inherited compounding direction</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<h3>Earthen Innovations (not directly from Titan)</h3>
+<table>
+<tr><th>Element</th><th>Earthen Form</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Notes</th></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Bael-</em></td><td><em>Baelgrim</em> (Stormward), <em>Bael'dun</em> (Dwarven)</td>
+    <td>stone / earth (?)</td><td>May be Earthen innovation or very early Titan morpheme; shared with Dwarven</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>-grim</em></td><td><em>Baelgrim</em></td>
+    <td>fierce / helmet (?)</td><td>Parallels Vrykul *-grim* in *Bjarngrim*; may be shared Titan morpheme</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Eir-</em></td><td><em>Eirich</em> (Machine Speaker)</td>
+    <td>guardian / healer (?)</td><td>Parallels Vrykul *Eyir* (Val'kyr); may be shared Titan morpheme or Norse design convergence</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Skar-</em></td><td><em>Skardyn</em> (corrupted Earthen)</td>
+    <td>dark / corrupt / shadow (?)</td><td>Parallels Vrykul *Skarvald*, *Voldskar*; may be shared Titan morpheme</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<h3>Earthen &harr; Dwarven: The Simplification Path</h3>
+
+<p>Dwarven is the daughter language of Earthen. The following table summarizes the
+phonological and morphological simplifications that occurred during the Earthen → Dwarven
+transition (driven by the Curse of Flesh):</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Feature</th><th>Earthen</th><th>Dwarven</th><th>Change</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Name length</td><td>Longer (*Baelgrim*, *Adelgonn*)</td><td>Shorter (*Magni*, *Brann*)</td><td>Reduction in morpheme count per name</td></tr>
+<tr><td>/θ/ phoneme</td><td>Present (*Brinthe*)</td><td>Absent from attested names</td><td>Loss of dental fricative</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Consonant clusters</td><td>High complexity (*Gundargaz*)</td><td>Moderate (*Khaz Modan*)</td><td>Cluster simplification</td></tr>
+<tr><td>*Khaz-* productivity</td><td>Productive prefix (*Khaz Algar*)</td><td>Fossilized proper name (*Khaz Modan*)</td><td>Morpheme fossilization</td></tr>
+<tr><td>*Bael-* morpheme</td><td>Productive in names (*Baelgrim*)</td><td>Restricted to toponym (*Bael'dun*)</td><td>Narrowing of usage</td></tr>
+</table>
+
