+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="qiraji">Qiraji Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="qiraji/grammar.md">qiraji/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: *Ahn-* toponymic prefix (shared with nerubian via Aqir substrate);
+*-qiraj* self-designation root; *-naxx* / *-axx* warrior suffix; apostrophe as morpheme boundary.
+Qiraji has <strong>no attested sentences at all</strong> — the entire corpus consists of proper names
+and place names. All constructions below are compound juxtapositions using inferred morphemes.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Qr1</td>
+  <td>Ahn'qiraj, Kurinnaxx.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈɑːnkwɪrɑːʒ ˈkʊrɪnæks/</td>
+  <td>Sacred-[people], [Kurinn]-warrior.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Ahn'qiraj* (fortress-temple) + attested *Kurinnaxx* (boss name); juxtaposition of place name and warrior name showing the *-naxx* suffix</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Qr2</td>
+  <td>Ahn'kahet, Ahn'qiraj.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈɑːnkɑːhɛt ˈɑːnkwɪrɑːʒ/</td>
+  <td>Old-kingdom, Sacred-[people].</td>
+  <td>Attested *Ahn'kahet* (nerubian) + attested *Ahn'qiraj* (qiraji); juxtaposition showing the shared *Ahn-* morpheme across two Aqir-descended languages</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Qr3</td>
+  <td>Rajaxx, Anubisath.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈrædʒɑːks ɑˈnuːbɪsæθ/</td>
+  <td>[Raj]-warrior, Guardian-[isath].</td>
+  <td>Attested *General Rajaxx* + attested *Anubisath*; juxtaposition of military leader and construct guardian names</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Qr4</td>
+  <td>Ovi'nax, Kurinnaxx.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈoʊvɪnæks ˈkʊrɪnæks/</td>
+  <td>[Ovi]-warrior, [Kurinn]-warrior.</td>
+  <td>Attested nerubian *Ovi'nax* + attested qiraji *Kurinnaxx*; juxtaposition showing the *-nax* / *-naxx* suffix across two Aqir-descended languages</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Qr5</td>
+  <td>Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈæʃi ˈzɔːrə/</td>
+  <td>Hive-[Ashi], Hive-[Zora].</td>
+  <td>Attested *Hive'Ashi* + attested *Hive'Zora*; juxtaposition of two silithid hive names showing the apostrophe compounding pattern</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Qr6</td>
+  <td>Ahn'qiraj, Azj-Kahet.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈɑːnkwɪrɑːʒ æzˈkɑːhɛt/</td>
+  <td>Sacred-[people], Deep-kingdom.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Ahn'qiraj* (qiraji) + attested *Azj-Kahet* (nerubian); juxtaposition of two Aqir-descended toponyms, showing both *Ahn-* and *Azj-* substrate morphemes</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<div class="warning">
+<strong>Reminder:</strong> None of these sentences appear in any Blizzard source. They are
+constructed to test the internal consistency of the inferred grammatical rules for
+Darnassian, Thalassian, Orcish, Shalassian, Draenei, Zandali, Taur-ahe, Dwarven,
+Titan, Vrykul, Nazja, Tol'vir, Drust, Mogu, Sethrak, Gnomish, Common, Shath'Yar, Kalimag,
+Earthen, Nerubian, and Qiraji.
+Any use of these sentences in fan works or scholarly analysis must clearly mark them as
+non-canon reconstructions.
+</div>
