 <h2 id="kobyss">Kobyss Naming (Hallowfall Creatures)</h2>
 
+<h2 id="oc-roc">Investigation: The *-oc* / *-roc* Element</h2>
+
+<p>Two Earthen names share the element *-oc* / *-roc*:</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Name</th><th>IPA</th><th>Context</th><th>Expansion</th></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Goggeroc</em></td><td class="ipa">/ˈɡɒɡərɒk/</td><td>Earthen (Kalimdor)</td><td>Classic (2004)</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Leikaroc</em></td><td class="ipa">/ˈleɪkærɒk/</td><td>Earthen NPC (Khaz Algar)</td><td>TWW (2024)</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<p>Possible decompositions: <em>Gogger-</em> + <span class="inferred">*-oc*</span>,
+or <em>Gogge-</em> + <span class="inferred">*-roc*</span>; <em>Leikar-</em> + <span class="inferred">*-oc*</span>
+or <em>Leika-</em> + <span class="inferred">*-roc*</span>.</p>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Assessment:</strong> Two attestations across 20 years of game development is suggestive
+but insufficient to confirm a genuine Earthen morpheme. No clear semantic pattern exists between
+the two bearers. The *-oc* / *-roc* ending may be a Blizzard aesthetic convention for harsh Earthen
+names rather than a genuine morpheme. If genuine, it could mean "stone/rock" or function as a
+personal name suffix.
+<br><br>
+<strong>Confidence: Very Low.</strong> Flagged for future investigation if additional *-oc* / *-roc*
+Earthen names are discovered in TWW patch content.
+</div>
+
 <p>The kobyss are monstrous amphibious creatures native to Hallowfall that attack during Beledar's
 Void phase. No individual kobyss NPC names are currently documented. The name "kobyss" may derive
 from Common "abyss" (co-abyss = "of the abyss"), a nerubian loanword, or an independent Arathi
 designation. <strong>Confidence: Very Low</strong> — no kobyss proper names or language data available.

