+
+<h3>Etymology: "Kobyss"</h3>
+
+<p>Four hypotheses:</p>
+<ol>
+<li><strong>Common "abyss"</strong>: *kobyss* ≈ "co-abyss" / "of the abyss" — Arathi designation</li>
+<li><strong>Ankoan-language</strong>: Could be an ankoan word (*Ko-byss*), but /ks/ in *-byss* doesn't match typical ankoan open-syllable phonotactics</li>
+<li><strong>Nerglish substrate</strong>: *-yss* could reflect gurgling phonology, but *ko-* is atypical of Nerglish</li>
+<li><strong>Independent Arathi</strong>: Unrelated to any known language family</li>
+</ol>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Confidence:</strong><br>
+&bull; <strong>Moderate</strong> for ankoan descent classification (wiki-confirmed lore)<br>
+&bull; <strong>Moderate</strong> for linguistic regression analysis (attested kobyss speech data confirms near-total language loss)<br>
+&bull; <strong>Low</strong> for Nerglish/murloc phonological analysis (limited to proper names)<br>
+&bull; <strong>Very Low</strong> for kobyss etymology (no native kobyss words attested)
+</div>
