 - **Nazja** (Naga) is derived from Darnassian but has diverged significantly due to 10,000 years of underwater isolation and physiological transformation
 - **Tol'vir** is likely derived from Titan, sharing this ancestry with **Mogu** — both are titan-forged languages from stone construct races; Tol'vir shows strong Egyptian-inspired naming conventions
 - **Ethereal / Broker** is spoken by ethereals and brokers from the shattered world of K'aresh; it has no confirmed genetic relationship to any other WoW language family. The potential *-esh* locative suffix appears in both *K'aresh* (homeworld) and *Tazavesh* (broker capital). Ethereals and brokers likely speak dialects of the same language, with broker names tending to be shorter. Despite sharing the apostrophe convention with Shath'Yar, nerubian, and qiraji, this is likely due to Blizzard design aesthetics rather than in-universe contact (see [alien-comparative.html](alien-comparative.html))
 - **Murloc/Jinyu/Ankoan/Kobyss** form a language family entirely separate from both the titan-forged and Aqir-descended families. Murlocs speak **Nerglish** (gurgling phonology, syllabic consonants); **Jinyu** evolved from murlocs with dramatically increased phonological complexity (full vowel inventory, CV/CVC syllable structure); **Ankoan** descend from jinyu with moderate simplification; **Kobyss** are ankoan-descended but show near-total language loss, retaining only 3–5 Common words ("Animate bones", "Devour", "Violence") — the only known case of linguistic regression in WoW (see [earthen/vocabulary.html](earthen/vocabulary.html#kobyss))
-- **Hara'ni** is spoken by the Haranir, an ancient race now confirmed to descend from **dark trolls/night elves** (*The Art of Midnight*, pg. 125): "those who would eventually become the haranir split from them and journeyed deep below the ground." This makes Hara'ni a **deeply divergent branch of the proto-troll/elven language family**, separated by ~16,000 years of independent development. No cognates with attested elven or troll languages are confirmed due to extreme time depth. The Haranir worship **Aln'hara** (the Worldsoul of Azeroth) as their goddess — confirmed by warcraft.wiki.gg. The **first confirmed Hara'ni translations** come from the wiki: *Shul'ka* = "Hunters of Shadows", *Har'alnor* = "Village of Twilight", *Har'athir* = "Village of Memory", *Har'kuai* = "Village of Rain", *Har'mara* = "Village of Balance". The morpheme **Har' = "village"** is confirmed by four independent attestations. The *Aln-* root has four attestations (*Aln'hara*, *Alndust*, *Alnscorned*, *Rift of Aln*) and likely means "deep/source/rift/essence"; **Alndust is confirmed to be Azerite** in particle form (warcraft.wiki.gg), and *Aln* is used as a verb in the quest title "The Greater They Aln." The *Hara-* root appears in five attestations (ethnonym, language name, capital, faction, concept) and likely means "people/we." The Shul'ka are Haranir warriors, healers, and guides who sever their connection to Aln'hara to patrol the Rift of Aln. The Zur'ashar are painter-storytellers. (see [haranir/](haranir/))
+- **Hara'ni** is spoken by the Haranir, an ancient race now confirmed to descend from **dark trolls/night elves** (*The Art of Midnight*, pg. 125): "those who would eventually become the haranir split from them and journeyed deep below the ground." This makes Hara'ni a **deeply divergent branch of the proto-troll/elven language family**, separated by ~16,000 years of independent development. No cognates with attested elven or troll languages are confirmed due to extreme time depth. The Haranir use the **same Xhosa-accented English as the Zandalari trolls**, suggesting inherited phonological features from proto-troll ancestry. The Haranir worship **Aln'hara** (the Worldsoul of Azeroth) as their goddess — confirmed by warcraft.wiki.gg. The **first confirmed Hara'ni translations** come from the wiki: *Shul'ka* = "Hunters of Shadows", *Har'alnor* = "Village of Twilight", *Har'athir* = "Village of Memory", *Har'kuai* = "Village of Rain", *Har'mara* = "Village of Balance". The morpheme **Har' = "village"** is confirmed by four independent attestations. The *Aln-* root has four attestations (*Aln'hara*, *Alndust*, *Alnscorned*, *Rift of Aln*) and likely means "deep/source/rift/essence"; **Alndust is confirmed to be Azerite** in particle form (warcraft.wiki.gg), and *Aln* is used as a verb in the quest title "The Greater They Aln." The *Hara-* root appears in five attestations (ethnonym, language name, capital, faction, concept) and likely means "people/we." The Shul'ka are Haranir warriors, healers, and guides who sever their connection to Aln'hara to patrol the Rift of Aln. The Zur'ashar are painter-storytellers. (see [haranir/](haranir/))

