+<h2 id="eredun">Eredun / Demonic Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="eredun/grammar.md">eredun/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: compounding (*draen* + *ei*, *Man'* + *ari*); apostrophe as morpheme boundary;
+*-ari* adjectival/nominal suffix; rhotic-heavy phonology. Eredun has <strong>no attested sentences</strong> —
+only proper names, title compounds, and decorative spell incantations. These sentences test compounding and suffix patterns.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Er1</td>
+  <td>Man'ari kil Argus.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/mɑnˈɑːrɪ kɪl ˈɑrgʊs/</td>
+  <td>The corrupt ones [destroyed/conquered] Argus.</td>
+  <td><em>Man'ari</em> (attested compound: Man + ari) + *kil* (inferred verb from <em>Kil'jaeden</em> element, meaning unknown) + <em>Argus</em>; <strong>highly speculative</strong> — *kil* is unattested as an independent verb</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Er2</td>
+  <td>Draen-ei, sha'tar.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈdreɪnaɪ ʃɑˈtɑr/</td>
+  <td>Exiled ones, born of light.</td>
+  <td>Attested compound <em>Draen-ei</em> (draen + ei) + attested compound <em>Sha'tar</em> (sha + tar); juxtaposition of two nominal phrases — no verb attested; <strong>moderate confidence</strong> in morphological decomposition</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Er3</td>
+  <td>Fel-or, man'ari.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/fɛlɔr mɑnˈɑːrɪ/</td>
+  <td>Corrupt world, the wrong ones.</td>
+  <td>Compound <em>Fel-or</em> (fel + or "world") + attested <em>Man'ari</em>; <strong>speculative</strong> — <em>fel</em> is only attested as an independent noun, not as a compound modifier</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Er4</td>
+  <td>Mac'Aree, draen-or.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/mɑkˈɑːrɪ ˈdreɪnɔr/</td>
