+<p>Shalassian phonology is inferred to resemble Darnassian and Thalassian: fluid consonants, vowel-heavy syllables, and melodic intonation. Apostrophes mark morpheme boundaries (<em>Shal'dorei</em>, <em>Shal'Aran</em>, <em>Ly'leth</em>). The language likely retains the five-vowel system /a e i o u/ of the elven family. No consonant clusters unusual for elven languages are attested.</p>
